<title>UK: Eastern plans venture with Celtic Energy.</title>
<headline>Eastern plans venture with Celtic Energy.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eastern Group, soon to be demerged from Hanson as part of Energy Group, is in talks with Welsh mining company Celtic Energy over developing a 400MW clean coal power station, said the Financial Times.</p>
<p>The newspaper said on Monday that the plant would be one of several Eastern is planning to build, including two further combined cycle gas-fired plants and an unspecified number of combined heat and power facilities.</p>
</text>
